   "Northwind-negotiator": "compromising",
   "Halcyon-researcher": "collaborating",
   "Halcyon-drafter": "competing",
   "Halcyon-negotiator": "competing"
  },
  "holistic_F_N": 1,
  "holistic_F_H": 1,
  "section_notes": "S1 requires all thermal events to be reported to regulators within 24 hours and affected customers notified within 72 hours. S2 sets a permanent 6.5% 55°C failure limit with no transition, gives per-model results to regulators and purchasers, but bars public per-model disclosure. S3 requires immediate remote shut-off on new models and feasible retrofits within six years; S4 requires built-in suppression at 36 months; S5 uses an 8/100k investigation/notice trigger but makes recall contingent on regulator assessment of corrective action."
 },
